{
  "about": "C19 (#884): Google event descriptions both sides read. `html` is whether a description is formatted rather than plain lines (the webview's looksLikeHtml, Rust's is_html). `supported` is whether PM's editor can write it back with nothing Google shows lost (the webview's parseDescription). `pm_can_edit` is the backend's laxer check (Rust's pm_can_edit: every tag one the editor writes, no comment, declaration or cut tag), which every supported row must pass, so the backend is never stricter than the webview. `legacy` is the names a browser reads without their ; (the webview's LEGACY, Rust's LEGACY_NAMES). `hrefs` is link addresses as written in an attribute, each `kept` when the webview's reader can write such a link back, the verdict Rust's pm_can_edit_unseen must give too. Synthesised strings only: nothing here is copied from a real person's calendar.",
